From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 21:19:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kk: MESA_KK_EXPERIMENTAL=gpl, a library's fragment shader
 compiled on its own

With MESA_KK_EXPERIMENTAL=gpl, a fragment shader alone in its pipeline
library (DXVK's fragment shader library) is now also compiled on its
own when the library is created, and its Metal library is built then
(kk_gpl_compile_fragment). Its MSL depends on no colour or depth format
(kk_lower_fs with gpl_separate):

- No blending in the shader (nir_lower_blend), no alpha to coverage or
  to one, no output signedness forced to the formats, no swizzle for
  non-native formats; every colour output is declared with 4
  components. Outputs keep their SPIR-V types.
- Dual-source blending's second source is declared
  [[color(0), index(1)]] (nir_to_msl_options::dual_source_blend).
- Depth writes stay unless early fragment tests are forced; depth
  clamp emulation is always in, driven by the root table's flag as
  before.
- No static sample mask: a draw whose sample mask is not all ones
  compiles the whole pipeline.
- User varyings are vec4s, as the vertex side's.

An empty fragment shader is compiled the same way once per device,
with the first vertex shader compiled on its own, for links without a
fragment shader.

A fast link of a vertex and a fragment shader both compiled on their
own now only builds the Metal render pipeline from the two libraries
(kk_gpl_link_libraries). Blending, the write masks and alpha to
coverage and to one are set on the pipeline's colour attachments and
multisample state from the draw's state (kk_gpl_set_fixed_function;
new bridge functions for MTL4RenderPipelineColorAttachmentDescriptor's
blend state and write mask and the descriptor's alpha to coverage and
to one), and the blend constants are set on the render encoder too.
Formats without blending are written without it. The link cache key
is as for G2's links.

Separately compiled stages match by their user varyings' names and
types, so the link checks the fragment shader's inputs against the
vertex shader's outputs and compiles the whole pipeline if one is not
written or has another type, or if the vertex shader writes cull
distances (the fragment shader does their discards). Links also
compile the whole pipeline, counted by reason on [kk-compile] link
lines, for: a logic op, an advanced blend op, a non-native colour
format, a colour output of a type the format cannot take, dual-source
blend factors without a second source (or with more than one colour
attachment), a depth write without a depth attachment, a sample mask
that is not all ones, alpha to coverage without colour output 0,
another view mask, and a fragment shader that reads input
attachments, gl_PrimitiveID or clip or cull distances, or indexes
varyings indirectly. A fragment shader that cannot be compiled on its
own otherwise (a written location 1 beside dual-source blending,
triangle merging that depends on the sample count on M1 and M2 before
OS 27, MESA_KK_DEBUG=solid, a compile or library failure) is compiled
at the first draw as before ([kk-compile] link separate-vertex
fragment=<reason>).

Pipelines that are not fast links, link-time-optimized ones included,
and everything without the flag compile as before, to the same MSL.

Linear: PLA-424
Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-21-kk-gpl-host.md
Offered-upstream: not yet
